 response←CreateRobotTxt request;txt;baseURL
⍝ Creates a file "robots.txt"
⍝ Nothing is disallowed, on purpose: a crawler must fetch a page in order to see a "noindex"
⍝ tag, and a page it is forbidden to fetch can still be indexed by its URL alone. A page that
⍝ should stay out of an index therefore carries "noindex" and stays fetchable; see
⍝ `search-engines.md`.
 txt←''
 txt,←⊂'User-agent: *'
 txt,←⊂'Crawl-delay: 10'        ⍝ Ignored by Google but honoured by Bing & Yandex & Yahoo at the time of writing (2024-12)
 :If HasSitemap
 :AndIf 0<≢baseURL←GetBaseURL request
     txt,←⊂''
     txt,←⊂'Sitemap: ',baseURL,'/sitemap.xml'
 :EndIf
 response←request ReturnTXT MassageTXT txt
⍝Done
